वृष m. man, husband, male of animals, esp. bull (old only
—˚), w. गवाम् the first of the dice;
 i.g. chief or best of (gen. or
—˚);
 E. of Śiva, Viṣṇu, etc., N. of sev. men.

वृष् व॑र्षति व॑र्ष˚ते pp. वृष्ट॑ (q.v.) rain (either
pers. w. Parjanya, Indra, etc. as subj., or impers.), pour down, shed or
cover with (instr.);
 loc. वर्षति while it is raining. C. वर्ष॑यति
cause to rain or let fall down as rain;
 sprinkle or cover with (instr.).
— अभि rain, pour down;
 sprinkle or cover with (instr.). अव & आ
the same. प्र begin to rain, pour or shower down;
 sprinkle or cover
with (instr.). प्रति, वि C., & सम् = prec. w. instr.

2 वृषध्वज a. having a bull for a sign;
 m. E. of
Śiva.

वृ॑षन् a. manly, potent, strong. m. man, stallion, bull,
boar, E. of sev. gods, esp. of Indra;
 f. वृष्णी mare.

वृषभ॑ a. manly, potent, strong;
 m. bull, first or best
of (gen. or —˚), chief, lord etc.

वृषा॑कपि m. strong ape or man-ape, a mythol. being;
 E.
of the sun, of Indra, etc.

वृष्णि॑ a. manly, potent, strong;
 m. ram, E. of Śiva etc.,
pl. N. of a princely race.

वृ॑ष्णि a. manly, potent, strong;
 m. ram, E. of Śiva etc.,
pl. N. of a princely race.

वृष्य a. causing manliness;
 m. E. of Śiva, n. an
aphrodisiac.
